# Feature Delivery — Evidence Ledger Schema

**Purpose:** Define a **machine-readable evidence ledger** so every claim in a Feature Delivery final report maps to a command, exit code, artifact, design record, research source, or capability status.

**Principle:** `initialHead` is a session baseline; `currentHead` **may change** after authorized commits on the locked branch.

---

## 1. Storage

| Item | Location |
| ---- | -------- |
| Session lock | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/SESSION.lock` |
| Baseline | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/baseline.json` |
| Requirements matrix | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/requirements-matrix.json` |
| Consumer map | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/consumer-and-boundary-map.json` |
| Data contract | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/data-contract-map.json` |
| Architecture review | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/architecture-review.json` |
| UI/UX decision | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/ui-ux-decision.json` |
| Test plan / realness | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/test-plan-and-realness.json` |
| Failure modes | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/failure-mode-analysis.json` |
| Bug hunt matrix | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/bug-hunt-matrix.json` |
| Bug reproduction | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/bug-reproduction.json` |
| Ledger (TSV) | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/evidence.tsv` |
| Design brief | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/design-brief.json` |
| Research | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/research.json` |
| Requirement queue | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/requirement-queue.json` |
| Blocker investigation | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/blocker-investigation.json` |
| Accepted risks | `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/accepted-risks.json` |

Phase C may add `scripts/agents/feature-delivery-evidence-ledger.mjs` to append rows. Phase A defines schema only.

---

## 2. SESSION.lock (JSON)

```json
{
  "sessionId": "<session-id>",
  "featureId": "<feature-slug>",
  "repoRoot": "/workspace",
  "lockedBranch": "<locked-branch>",
  "initialHead": "<initial-head-sha>",
  "currentHead": "<initial-head-sha>",
  "startedAt": "2026-09-04T04:55:00.000Z",
  "scopePaths": ["apps/api/src/workspace-<module>/**", "docs/phase-<feature-slug>/**"],
  "checkpointsCompleted": ["CP0", "CP1", "CP2"]
}
```

| Field          | Semantics                                                                       |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `lockedBranch` | Immutable for session — hard-stop if `git branch --show-current` differs        |
| `initialHead`  | Recorded at bootstrap — evidence baseline only                                  |
| `currentHead`  | Updated after each authorized commit — **allowed to change**                    |
| `scopePaths`   | Glob allowlist for staged files at CP4 — **derived per feature session** at CP0 |

---

## 3. evidence.tsv columns

Tab-separated header (required):

```
session_id	feature_id	locked_branch	initial_head	current_head	checkpoint	gate_id	command	exit_code	artifact	result	verifier	timestamp
```

| Column          | Type    | Description                                                   |
| --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `session_id`    | string  | Matches `SESSION.lock.sessionId`                              |
| `feature_id`    | string  | Stable feature slug                                           |
| `locked_branch` | string  | Branch at time of row (must match lock)                       |
| `initial_head`  | string  | Session baseline SHA (constant per session)                   |
| `current_head`  | string  | `git rev-parse HEAD` when row recorded — **may advance**      |
| `checkpoint`    | enum    | `D0`–`D7`, `B1`–`B8`, legacy `CP0`–`CP7`, `bootstrap`, `report` |
| `gate_id`       | string  | Stable id e.g. `guard.import-boundary`, `test.<package-name>` |
| `command`       | string  | Exact shell command run                                       |
| `exit_code`     | int     | `0` = pass; non-zero = fail/skip documented in `result`       |
| `artifact`      | string  | Path to log, screenshot, json report; empty if stdout-only    |
| `result`        | enum    | `pass` \| `fail` \| `skip` \| `blocked`                       |
| `verifier`      | string  | `agent` \| `architecture-reviewer` \| `script` \| `user`      |
| `timestamp`     | ISO8601 | UTC                                                           |

### 3.1 Example rows

```tsv
session_id	feature_id	locked_branch	initial_head	current_head	checkpoint	gate_id	command	exit_code	artifact	result	verifier	timestamp
fda-001	<feature-slug>	<locked-branch>	abc12345	abc12345	CP0	bootstrap.git-status	git status --short --branch	0		pass	agent	2026-09-04T04:55:01Z
fda-001	<feature-slug>	<locked-branch>	abc12345	abc12345	CP4	guard.import-boundary	pnpm run guard:import-boundary	0		pass	script	2026-09-04T05:10:00Z
fda-001	<feature-slug>	<locked-branch>	abc12345	def67890	CP4	commit	fix(<scope>): <summary>	0		pass	agent	2026-09-04T05:12:00Z
```

After an authorized commit (`def67890`), `current_head` in `SESSION.lock` and subsequent rows reflects the new SHA while `initial_head` stays `abc12345`. **HEAD advancement on `lockedBranch` is expected** — not a branch-lock violation.

---

## 4. arch-review.json

Architecture-reviewer output (read-only phase). Schema per [architecture-reviewer](../../.cursor/agents/architecture-reviewer.md) — includes `researchSources`, `designFindings`, `missingEvidence`, `stopId`, `requiredDecision`, `recommendedNextStep`.

```json
{
  "sessionId": "<session-id>",
  "featureId": "<feature-slug>",
  "checkpoint": "CP3",
  "classifierProposal": "module",
  "verdict": "pivot",
  "consumers": ["<domain-a>", "<domain-b>", "<domain-c>"],
  "researchSources": [],
  "designFindings": [{ "severity": "warning", "summary": "Missing denied state for CAP-002" }],
  "missingEvidence": ["browser proof for CAP-001"],
  "platformCandidates": ["notifications"],
  "finding": "Module-specific persistence duplicates shared primitive",
  "stopId": "SC-ARCH-02",
  "requiredDecision": "Accept module-local v1 or pivot to platform inbox",
  "recommendedNextStep": "Update design brief §8 before CP4",
  "reviewer": "architecture-reviewer",
  "timestamp": "2026-09-04T04:56:00.000Z"
}
```

---

## 5. Extended gate_id conventions (v1.2)

| Prefix | Example | Binds to |
| ------ | ------- | -------- |
| `research.` | `research.RES-001` | `research.json` entry |
| `bug-hunt.` | `bug-hunt.B3` | `bug-hunt-matrix.json` / `bug-reproduction.json` |
| `design.` | `design.baseline` | `baseline.json` |
| `design.` | `design.requirements-matrix` | `requirements-matrix.json` |
| `design.` | `design.consumer-map` | `consumer-and-boundary-map.json` |
| `design.` | `design.data-contract` | `data-contract-map.json` |
| `design.` | `design.failure-modes` | `failure-mode-analysis.json` |
| `design.` | `design.test-realness` | `test-plan-and-realness.json` |
| `browser.` | `browser.CAP-003` | Screenshot / recording artifact |
| `uiux.` | `uiux.decision` | `ui-ux-decision.json` |
| `uiux.promax.` | `uiux.promax.member-wallet` | UI UX Pro Max search stdout |
| `capability.` | `capability.CAP-001` | Requirement inventory status |
| `blocker.` | `blocker.BR-CODE-001` | `blocker-investigation.json` |
| `arch-review` | `arch-review.CP1` | `arch-review.json` |

---

## 6. Required gates by feature touch

| Touch surface       | Minimum `gate_id` rows before push                                                    |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Any code            | `bootstrap.branch`, `git.diff-check`, `pre-commit.fast` or documented hook suspension |
| `apps/api` / Prisma | `guard.repository-rls`, `guard.api-workspace-isolation`, targeted postgres spec       |
| Protected packages  | `guard.docs`, `doc.markdoc.validate`                                                  |
| UI                  | app `build`, Playwright smoke, **browser** screenshots desktop+mobile, accessibility when available, `ui-ux-decision.json` for visible features |
| Platform candidate  | `arch-review.json` with reviewer `verdict` at CP1, CP3, CP4, CP7 |
| Design gate         | `design-brief.json` + `design.brief`; `ui-ux-decision.json` + `uiux.decision` for visible UI |
| Research            | `research.<id>` row per external source used |

Skipped gates must be `result: skip` with reason in artifact or `gate_id` suffix (e.g. `browser.CAP-003.skip-no-env`).

---

## 7. test-changed coverage gap (feature-scoped)

**When it applies:** Only when the **current feature session** changes files under a package path that [`scripts/test-changed.sh`](../../../scripts/test-changed.sh) does not map (e.g. `packages/<package-name>/*` missing from `pkg_for_path`).

**When it does not apply:** Unrelated features or packages not touched in the session — no global blocker.

If a gap affects the current feature, the agent must:

1. Add ledger row `gate_id=test-changed.coverage-gap` with `result=blocked` (feature-scoped)
2. Run explicit `<targeted-test-command>` — e.g. `pnpm --filter @app-tour/<package-name> test` — and record a separate row with `result=pass` or `fail`
3. Note the gap in the final report until Phase D fixes the path map

**Unverified claims are forbidden** — e.g. "`<package-name>` 75/75" without a ledger row for the exact command.

---

## 8. blocker-investigation.json

Per [blocker-recovery](blocker-recovery.mdoc) §5. One artifact per recovered or exhausted blocker.

**Required fields:** `blockerId`, `category`, `symptoms`, `localEvidence`, `codeAnalysis`, `searches`, `hypotheses`, `commandsRun`, `outcomes`, `decision`, `resumedCheckpoint`, `timestamp`.

Link to ledger via `gate_id=blocker.<blockerId>`.

| `decision`  | Meaning                                                      |
| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `recovered` | Fix or env remediation applied; queue resumed                |
| `hard_stop` | Escalated to STOP report — no further recovery               |
| `deferred`  | Row stays `UNVERIFIED`/`BLOCKED`; other queue items continue |

---

## 9. Final report binding

Each report section must cite ledger rows or session artifacts:

| Report claim          | Required evidence                                                  |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Branch unchanged      | `bootstrap.branch` + pre-push `git branch --show-current`          |
| Tests passed          | Row per suite with `exit_code=0`                                   |
| Tests skipped         | Row with `result=skip` — matrix stays **UNVERIFIED**, not COMPLETE |
| RLS verified          | Postgres spec row + `guard.repository-rls`                         |
| Architecture approved | `arch-review.json` `verdict: proceed`                            |
| Design gate complete  | `design-brief.json` + `design.brief` ledger row                    |
| Research used         | `research.json` + `research.<id>` rows                             |
| Browser verified      | `browser.<capabilityId>` + artifact path — **not** curl alone    |
| UI browser verified   | `browser.<capabilityId>` + BQC realness class `real-e2e` or documented `partial` |
| UI accessibility      | `browser.a11y.<capabilityId>` or axe log artifact                |
| UI UX Pro Max used    | `uiux.promax.<slug>` — only when search command ran              |
| UI decision gate      | `uiux.decision` + `ui-ux-decision.json`                          |
| Capability complete   | `capability.<id>` with status `tested` or `browser-verified`       |
| Admin mutation works  | Browser or API proof with permission + audit ledger rows           |
| Blocker recovered     | `blocker-investigation.json` + `gate_id=blocker.<id>` rows         |
| Design stages complete | `baseline.json`, `requirements-matrix.json`, tier-required D-artifacts |
| Adversarial passes | `bug-hunt-matrix.json` + `bug-hunt.B*` ledger rows |
| Verdict | `evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs` pass + `FEATURE_*` aligned to matrix |
| Commits               | Rows with `gate_id=commit` and SHAs matching `git log`             |

**Forbidden without evidence:** COMPLETE with open rows; admin usability from read-only catalog; browser success from API/curl; production readiness from local tests only; UI UX Pro Max cited without `uiux.promax.*` ledger row.

---

## 10. ui-ux-decision.json

**Location:** `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/ui-ux-decision.json`

**Required for:** every user-visible feature at CP1 before source implementation.

```json
{
  "featureId": "<feature-slug>",
  "surface": "portal|web|marketing",
  "actor": "member|operator-owner|operator-viewer|guest|platform-admin",
  "placement": { "kind": "repository-convention", "summary": "...", "justification": "..." },
  "informationArchitecture": { "existingSurfaces": [], "newTabJustification": null },
  "designSystemSource": ["design-system/tokens", "docs/phase-2-design-system.md"],
  "uiUxProMaxUsed": true,
  "uiUxProMaxRecommendations": [
    { "query": "tour operator dashboard", "command": "python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py ...", "kind": "design-recommendation", "summary": "..." }
  ],
  "repositoryConstraints": [
    { "kind": "repository-convention", "ref": "docs/dev/semantic-color-contract.mdoc", "summary": "Use semantic tokens only" }
  ],
  "selectedDecisions": [
    { "section": "placement", "kind": "product-requirement", "decision": "..." }
  ],
  "rejectedAlternatives": [
    { "alternative": "New top-level tab", "reason": "Fits existing registrations area", "kind": "inference" }
  ],
  "responsiveRules": { "desktop": "...", "mobile": "..." },
  "rtlLtrRules": { "fa": "...", "en": "..." },
  "accessibilityRules": { "keyboard": "...", "aria": "..." },
  "requiredBrowserEvidence": ["desktop screenshot", "mobile RTL", "BQC spec path"],
  "conflicts": [],
  "unresolvedDecisions": [],
  "reviewerVerdict": "pending|approve|approve_with_gaps|reject"
}
```

### 10.1 UI evidence status (final report)

| Status | Meaning |
| ------ | ------- |
| `ui-designed` | `ui-ux-decision.json` + design brief complete |
| `ui-implemented` | Source merged within scope |
| `ui-tested` | Unit/contract tests pass with ledger rows |
| `ui-browser-verified` | BQC real browser proof with artifacts |
| `ui-accessibility-verified` | axe or equivalent with artifact |
| `ui-production-verified` | Staging/production proof with explicit unlock |
| `ui-accepted-risk` | Documented gap with architect acceptance |
| `ui-unverified` | Missing browser, a11y, or environment evidence |

Never claim `ui-browser-verified` from build, API 200, or screenshot without interaction.

